flowchart LR
  accTitle: Windows PATH truncation and harness auto-repair flow
  accDescr: Windows Registry holds both Machine and User PATH values, which commonly exceed 2047 characters on developer workstations. Explorer and legacy launchers silently truncate or drop User PATH when starting IDEs and harnesses. Third-party harnesses detect and refresh PATH per session or command, while DevCentr Harness checks on process launch, repairs process PATH from Registry, and surfaces an in-app alert with a link to remediation docs.
  reg["Windows Registry\nHKLM Machine + HKCU User PATH\n(often > 2,047 chars)"]
  exp["Explorer / legacy launcher\n2,047-char truncation bug\n(silently drops User PATH)"]
  third["Third-party AI harnesses\n(Cursor, Antigravity, Claude Code)\nStart-of-conversation check +\nRegistry refresh per shell"]
  dc["DevCentr Harness\nCheck on process launch\nRead HKLM + HKCU Registry\nAuto-repair process PATH"]
  ui["In-app UI alert\nReport fix or error +\nlink to reference doc"]
  perm["Permanent fix\nTrim duplicates & missing dirs\n(pathman / short junctions)"]

  reg --> exp
  exp -. "truncated env block" .-> third
  exp -. "truncated env block" .-> dc
  reg --> dc
  dc --> ui
  third --> perm
  ui --> perm

  class reg primary
  class exp danger
  class third warning
  class dc success
  class ui secondary
  class perm secondary
